<title>BRAZIL: Foreigners to pay Brazil CPMF tax on investments.</title>
<headline>Foreigners to pay Brazil CPMF tax on investments.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors will pay a 0.2 percent charge under Brazil's co-called CPMF tax on starting and ending investments on the country's stock exchanges, a finance ministry official said.</p>
<p>But investors would not pay the CPMF on transactions in between the start and finish of those investments, Pedro Parente, the ministry's executive secretary, said.</p>
<p>The new tax, which is aimed at raising $400 million a month for Brazil's public health service, comes into effect on January 25.</p>
<p>Government officials had expressed concern that the CPMF might discourage foreign investors from buying Brazilian stocks and had sought ways of reducing the net cost of the tax to foreigners.</p>
</text>
